## Context

Child of tickets/1004. The statistics policy (spec §7) is idle without
defect-bearing games. The audition board's `defects:` anchors are empty on
all 10 entries, so UVER is pinned at 0 by construction; the live trial's
diffs were mostly clean and gate-cleared.

## Actions

1. Backfill `defects:` anchors on the frozen board
   (skills/reviewers/benchmark-board.yml) from confirmed panel misses:
   post-merge fixes, follow-up tickets, later-found regressions.
2. Mine defect-bearing merged PRs across projects (the 0356 sample):
   PRs whose defect was confirmed post-merge become new labeled board
   entries — same frozen base/head SHA discipline.
3. Ten labeled defect-bearing games per seat resolve a 50%-vs-0% catch
   gap (Fisher p ≈ 0.03); ~60 per pair for fine distinctions (spec §7).
   Seed toward the coarse bar first.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All board entries carry a populated or explicitly-empty defects
      set, with the empty case justified per entry
- [ ] At least 10 defect-bearing games exist for the primary incumbent
      seat (openrouter-frontier successor) to be ranked against

2026-10-02T08:37Z claude note Raid Imagine + Blind-Spot pass 2026-10-02: annotation appended; premise confirmed at HEAD 108c3cd7 (board unchanged, 1008 unblocked by PR #1115); mining narrowed to a manual pass over this repo's history first, cross-project replay machinery split to a follow-up.

## Imagine annotation (raid 2026-10-02)

Premise holds at HEAD 108c3cd7: all 10 board entries still carry empty
`defects:`, nothing on the board or classifier changed since creation, and
1008 is the only ready child of 1004 (unblocked by PR #1115).

Simplest path, exit criteria unchanged:

- **Backfill of the frozen 10 is a justification exercise, not discovery.**
  Sweep PRs 570-603 for confirmed misses (citing tickets, later fix commits
  touching their lines); expected honest outcome is explicitly-empty defects
  with a per-entry justification. Nearest signals do not attach: 0324 closed
  via PR #567 before the board PRs; 0333's #584 incident was ruled UNCONFIRMED.
- **Criterion 2 is met by appending mined defect-bearing entries from THIS
  repo's history** (post-merge fix commits, revert-following fixes, follow-up
  tickets citing merged PRs, projects/**/memory incident records naming this
  repo's PRs), keeping the single-repo invariant the audition consumer relies
  on. Prefer code-heavy diffs; the incumbent seat reviews code.
- **NARROWING (allowed):** manual/agent-assisted mining with a mechanical
  prefilter, no committed scripted pipeline. 0356's classifier, challenger-
  vs-squad mode and stopping rules are 1007/coaching-skill scope.
- **Anchor rule (pre-registered):** defect anchors are `basename:LINE` in the
  head SHA's file version, mapped back from the confirming fix commit;
  degrade to `basename:*` when the line mapping is not mechanical. Every
  anchor carries recorded confirming evidence (fix commit SHA or citing
  ticket) in the PR body, not in the YAML comments (agnostic-gate literals).

Constraints from the Blind-Spot pass (all verified against the tree):

1. **Cross-project entries are unreplayable today.** `audition` hard-codes
   `--repo "$REPO_ROOT"` (reviewers.sh:713) and the board schema has no repo
   field; foreign SHAs would fail-loud on every replay. Cross-project mining
   therefore does NOT append to the shipped board: if this repo's history
   yields fewer than 10, the shortfall is recorded with candidate evidence
   and replay machinery goes to a follow-up ticket (repo field + seat-runner
   repo resolution), never into this ticket's board edit.
2. **Board size is test-asserted**: tests/test_reviewers_audition.sh asserts
   `board=10MR` on the shipped board; extending the board must update that
   assertion. Historical 10MR scorecards stay comparable by size-matching
   (SLOW gate peers match on board size).
3. **`pr` is the only entry key** (reviewers.sh:707) — appended entries must
   not duplicate a PR number already on the board.
4. **The incumbent has never played any board** — no audition scorecard
   exists for the primary OpenRouter seat. Criterion 2 ships labeled games;
   the incumbent's replay run over the extended board (model id pinned) is a
   separate activity, filed as a follow-up, not exit criteria here.

