## Plan annotation (raid 2026-10-02)

### Actions

1. Sweep the frozen 10 (justification, not discovery). Per board PR (570, 572,
   573, 575, 580, 584, 588, 599, 602, 603): find its merge commit MC
   (`git log --merges --format='%H %s' | grep '#<PR> '`), base=MC^1, head=MC^2;
   grep tickets/ and memory/ for citations; list post-merge commits touching
   the PR's changed files and filter fix-ish subjects; adjudicate each
   candidate with the CONFIRMED rule below before populating `defects:`.
   Known negatives stay empty: PR 584's 0333 incident ruled UNCONFIRMED;
   0324/#567 predates the board.
2. CONFIRMED rule: a defect is confirmed iff (a) a fix commit F merged on main
   strictly after MC whose fixed pre-image lines blame to a commit I with
   `git merge-base --is-ancestor I head && ! --is-ancestor I base`, or (b) a
   closed follow-up ticket citing the PR whose fix passes (a).
3. Empty defects carry a justification comment on its own line ABOVE the
   `defects:` key (never inline — reviewers.sh `fv()` would parse it into the
   anchor field), containing the token `none confirmed`, phrased to pass
   check-agnostic.sh (no forge URLs, no repo-relative script paths, no
   absolute home paths).
4. Mine >=10 defect-bearing merged PRs from THIS repo's history: `fix`-subject
   commits with blame-based introduction attribution; closed tickets citing
   merged PRs; memory incident records. Accept only merge-commit PRs, code-
   heavy diffs, pr not already on the board, CONFIRMED defects. Shortfall is
   recorded honestly; cross-project machinery goes to a follow-up ticket.
5. Anchor rule (pre-registered): head-SHA `basename:LINE` (direct line
   transfer when the file is untouched between head and fix^, else
   blame-mapped, else degrade to `basename:*`). Confirming evidence (fix SHA
   or citing ticket) recorded in the implementing PR body, not the YAML.
6. Append entries after PR 603 in the same scalar format; populate `panel:`
   from gate-verdict comments when accessible, else record the gap in the PR
   body; pr values unique.
7. Update tests/test_reviewers_audition.sh: replace the hard-coded
   `board=10MR` assertion with the dynamic count (`grep -cE '^[[:space:]]*-
   [[:space:]]*pr:'`) and tighten the board-size floor.
8. Gates: new test file + `make check` (check-agnostic, check-personal-data,
   check-skills-drift, check-tests).

### First test (red before the board edit)

New `tests/test_benchmark_board.sh`, auto-discovered by
tests/test_bash_suites.py:
- (a) every entry block has a `defects:` key; empty value requires a
  `none confirmed` justification comment in the block;
- (b) anchors verified against git history: basename present in
  `git diff --name-only base...head`; line-precise anchors blame inside the
  PR (ancestry vs base/head) — oracle independent of the YAML;
- (c) pr values unique;
- (d) RED driver: entries with non-empty `defects:` >= 10 (exit criterion 2).
(a)-(c) are regression guards passing today; (d) goes green only when labeled
entries land. Do not land (d) without (b) — the count alone is satisfiable by
fabrication; the pair is not.

### Dependencies

None (1008 unblocked by PR #1115; single-repo invariant kept).

### Antipattern scan (tautology)

(a),(b),(c) each catch distinct failure classes (dropped key / fabricated or
drifted anchor / findings-file overwrite via duplicate pr); the board-size
re-assertion is derived from the file, not a new literal. (d) alone would be
tautology-prone; paired with (b) it is not.

